{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/423285-building-a-trinity-era-nova-sane-ones-please","id":423285,"title":"Building a Trinity Era Nova (sane ones please)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-28T12:18:23-08:00","id":423285,"title":"Building a Trinity Era Nova (sane ones please)","content":"Basically, how do you define a Node Brain in game terms. Let's say my Nova has contacted your Psions in Deep space. (I.E. I joined you campaign several weeks in). How many Nova points and freebe points do I get? And what do a spend just to be a sane Nova?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:06:55-08:00","id":424683,"title":"","content":"I don't know what you mean by a &quot;node brain&quot;.<br /> So in this scenario, a psionic survey team is contacted, star-trek style by a mysterious entity of great power and seemingly benevolent, they are going to let it on board and team up with it? Exactly how many of these psions paid any attention to Aberrant hysteria or adventure tropes growing up in the late 2100's? Because the whole thing could fall apart right there. Expect more incoming fire than incoming replies.<br /> But, i can't talk, i tried this once before myself and so i must warn you strongly against it - if you are a player coming into another's game you should warn them too. But, no testimony i give is going to better the mechanism to prove it to yourself.<br /> First and most important question is; why do this as opposed to adding a character better balanced for the system? The <b>Stalwart</b> of Adventure! would be a better ruleset to utilize, if you have to do it this way, simply for balance. I don't know what would be needed to survive in deep-space like you suggest, but a decently crafted pod might sustain a mighty stalwart for quite some time in the void - Captain America style. If you can do that, do that instead - the rules will release a sigh of relief. If you can create a character free of the need of Quantum distinction from the rest of the party, do that first - our characters are roles, not power-sets.<br /> Second question is; where did this 'Nova' come from? Why are they in deep space to be encountered there and how long have they been there for? If the answer to the last question is greater than a year or so, they will need social and mental adaptions for the isolation and sensory deprivation. You want Mega Charisma's <b>Autonomy</b> (Forceful Personalities p90), something like Mega-Wit's <b>Unfazeable</b> from Brainwaves (p52), whatever your ST wants you to take for physically surviving in space - if longer than a year, maximized <b>mega-stamina</b> might be needed to hold your breath (or just not breathe) for long enough. So, maybe a <b>physical alteration</b>, or some inexpensive way to fend off the temperature extremes like <b>Armor</b>. If you were under propulsion in space, you'll need to explain that -<b> flight </b>will do. If you were headed somewhere through space, then some level of <b>mega-perception</b> and maybe <b>mega-intelligence</b> would keep you on course - but even the shortest distances would be a nightmare journey without machine instruments to discern distances and time.<br /> Again, the ST will have the final say on what you need to survive their vision of vacuum - maybe add <b>Sensory Shield</b> into the mix or something i'm not thinking of. Oh, and of course <b>Taint Resistance</b> (Player's Guide p76). You need it or you are guaranteed to be a lost cause before you begin, with Taint equal to your starting Quantum - but i think it's bundled for the suggestion below.<br /> The best balance for 2008 era Novas in 2120 are the '<b>Asia Ascendant</b>' web-supplement's <b>Low Quantum</b> versions on page 72, but rather than me repeat that here, go out and give it a hit where-ever it's posted these days. Follow those rules, i can't emphasize this enough - beyond that lies ruin and despair for the game balance. But stick to the low Quantum rules and be prepared to be hunted until the end of your days for showing your face and you can get a few games worth of tolerable cross-over, i'm sure. It's worth noting that the Asia Ascendant rules still aren't as preferable as the Stalwart system from Adventure!. But they avoid inspiration points if that's the desired result.<br /> I'm not looking at the prices or doing any math, but i'll bet you can't afford the character with those resources. This is intentional - the kind of Nova you seem to be talking about is a league above the level of Nova that can safely cross-over with a party of Chamber Psions without scarring their sense of self-value. Your mileage may vary as the player of said Nova, obviously, but it would be a cruel trick to pull on an unsuspecting ST. I did it to myself and still consider it a cruel trick.<br /> <br /> If the nova in question wasn't a player, this scenario would be rather more appealing as an adventure for the psions. If you are their first space aberrant and you come to the airlock with a smile and a hard-luck story - you may irrepairably damage the universe (read: 2120 setting) for them in the process. What dividends can you yield that surpass an encounter with one of the possibilities &quot;free-floating space nova&quot; could entail? Think about this, because it's a dramatic departure from likely player expectations if i have the details correct. If you can spin a fun tale on the way in, it could be forgiveable, if still jarring - but you have to work with the ST for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Added specific powers and emphasis 03-01-2015, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:08:39-08:00","id":426908,"title":"","content":"I never knew that &quot;Forceful Personalities&quot; or &quot;Brainwave&quot; got published. Were do you find these books. Are they on Drive Thru RPG?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T16:08:07-08:00","id":427081,"title":"","content":"I'm stil not certain how the linking works here, or whether posting links to unofficial sources are against any rules.<br /> I can't even figure out how to post more than one link, so istead i'm going to just supply to raw URLs.<br /> -shame-<br /> <br /> FP: <a href=\"http://suptg.thisisnotatrueending.com/archive/30369244/images/1392905442173.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://suptg.thisisnotatrueending.co...2905442173.pdf</a><br /> BW: <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/files/file/1-aberrant-brainwaves/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.rpgpost.com/files/file/1-...nt-brainwaves/</a><br /> ABA: <a href=\"http://soulfire.net/Aberrant/Aberrant%20-%20Sup%20-%20A%20Breed%20Apart.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://soulfire.net/Aberrant/Aberran...ed%20Apart.pdf</a><br /> <br /> I might be missing somethings (please, let me know if i am), but there were a few belated gifts to the community since the lines were cancelled - all requiring ST oversight before dragging them into a new game. None of these sources should be dragged out to dump onto a Trinity ST without their uncorrupted consent - these are unofficial rules for Aberrant and balancing with psions and the 2120 setting wasn't necessarily a high priority.<br /> <br /> I'm getting the distinct impression that i'm arming some kind of military coup against an existing game - please don't use these suggestions in that manner, Astromancer.<br /> -smile-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Apparently linking works automatically of URLs, a mystery is solved. 03-03-2015, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T16:18:27-08:00","id":427088,"title":"","content":"Just missing TNF: <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/files/file/55-aberrant-the-new-flesh/\" target=\"_blank\">The New Flesh</a> the physical one to go with BW and FP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4074-sreden","name":"Sreden","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T16:21:52-08:00","id":427090,"title":"","content":"&quot;Forceful Personalities&quot; and &quot;A Breed Apart&quot; were a fan books. FP was based on the planned-but-cancelled concept of a book on Mega-Social novas.<br /> <br /> &quot;Brainwaves&quot; (Mega-Mental novas) was contracted, but only got to the first draft stage before Aberrant was cancelled, so whether or not it counts as &quot;official&quot; is an exercise up to the reader.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T19:01:56-08:00","id":427228,"title":"","content":"Ah, the new flesh was completed! I have some saved notes from the creation process.<br /> -rubs hands together-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/423285-building-a-trinity-era-nova-sane-ones-please?p=427090#post427090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Forceful Personalities&quot; and &quot;A Breed Apart&quot; were a fan books. FP was based on the planned-but-cancelled concept of a book on Mega-Social novas.<br /> <br /> &quot;Brainwaves&quot; (Mega-Mental novas) was contracted, but only got to the first draft stage before Aberrant was cancelled, so whether or not it counts as &quot;official&quot; is an exercise up to the reader.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for clearing that up - i've tended to focus on the setting rather than the development over my time, these things commonly excape me if the material fits well enough.<br /> This might be the wrong thread however...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T22:45:35-07:00","id":481126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/423285-building-a-trinity-era-nova-sane-ones-please?p=427090#post427090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Forceful Personalities&quot; and &quot;A Breed Apart&quot; were a fan books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reading through &quot;A Breed Apart&quot; now and it looks and reads like an official Aberrant book, even though I know its a fan book. Whoever wrote this book <i>really </i>did his homework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"